direction: down
title: "GAMBIT MODERNIZATION FOUNDATION\nModern C is mandatory; Zig is a conditional implementation evolution"
title.shape: text
scheme: "Gambit Scheme semantic owner\nBindings / evaluation / tail calls / closures\nGeneral continuations / dynamic-wind / foreign effects"
contract: "One explicit compiler / runtime contract\nVM and execution rights; root / object update law\nFrames / control / resumption; sharing / memory model\nGC participation; resources / code / actual last use"
modern: "Mandatory modern generated C foundation\nPreserved C backend / ABI / FFI / embedding\nTyped interfaces and explicit ownership / failure paths\nOne implementation owner per selected mechanism"
multicore: "Execution and scheduling\nWorkers differ from suspended contexts and VMs\nParallelism differs from effects-based concurrency"
gc: "Memory and GC\nNursery / mature / pinned; all write and root producers\nPromotion / barriers / parked roots / independent GC work"
control: "Control and native boundary\nGeneral continuation plus researched one-shot effects path\nNo accidental capture of C frames or native resources"
llvm: "Independent LLVM / MLIR services\nLegal high-level transforms, code generation / debug\nProducts and invalidation separate from mutable instances"
zig: "Possible C-to-Zig change for a NAMED implementation\nPreserve C contract; prove concrete support removed\nCount compiler / ABI / tooling / upgrade / migration cost\nRetire old owner; no default duplicate implementation"
gate: "Required capability + semantic / resource qualification\nCommon modernization benefit != Zig-specific benefit\nNo implementation or native acceptance in this study"
scheme -> contract -> modern
modern -> multicore
modern -> gc
modern -> control
contract -> llvm
modern -> zig: "replacement hypothesis, not adopted layer"
multicore -> gate
gc -> gate
control -> gate
llvm -> gate
zig -> gate
modern.style.fill: "#E8F4E8"
contract.style.fill: "#DFEEFF"
zig.style.fill: "#FFF0E5"
